## 1. Original contributions: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International

Everything produced for this compilation is released under **CC BY 4.0**.
You may share and adapt it, including commercially, provided you give
appropriate credit, link to the license, and indicate if changes were made.

Canonical legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This covers:

- All 56 images in `assets/art/`: the illustrations and the diagram plates
  for every volume
- The whole text of Volumes 2, 3 and 4 (`desktop/`, `bots/`, `company/`
  and their sources under `src/volumes/`), including every prompt, table
  and template in them
- The whole of the Build Track: the introduction, Builds 0 through 10,
  the ledger, and every prompt, template, config block and table in them
- The consolidated reference tables, including the constants table
  (Appendix C) and the failure-triage table (Appendix D)
- The vocabulary table and the twelve operator drills
- The 30/60/90 adoption path (Appendix E)
- Appendices F, G and H in full: the SOUL.md and USER.md guidance and
  worked files, the skills and plugins examples, and the worked build
  prompts and template
- The structural editing, cross-references and section organization

Attribution for this layer: **Jason Jeske**, from the repository
`jasonjeske/hermes-master-class`.

---

## 2. Underlying source material: not licensed by this repository

The substance of Parts 1 through 12 is the work of **Tony Simons**
([@tonysimons_](https://x.com/tonysimons_)), published as the twelve-part
*Hermes Agent Master Class* on X between July 5 and July 20, 2026.

He published it free and without a paywall, and it is reproduced here as a
study reference with credit. That is the extent of what this repository
asserts. **It does not relicense his work, and CC BY 4.0 above does not
extend to it.** Rights in the underlying articles remain entirely with their
author.

If you want to reuse the source material itself rather than this
compilation's additions, the source articles are linked per-part in
[Appendix I](masterclass/appendix-i-sources.md), and the author is the person
to ask.

The original article artwork is deliberately not reproduced anywhere in this
repository.

The Build Track and Volumes 2 to 4 quote short passages of the official
Hermes Agent documentation, of bundled files from the Hermes Agent repository,
and of the Hindsight and Mnemosyne READMEs where a template had to match the
documented shape exactly. Volumes 3 and 4 quote short passages from named
operators' public videos and posts, credited in place and in ATTRIBUTION.md;
those words remain theirs. Hermes Agent is
published by Nous Research under the MIT License; those passages remain
theirs and are credited in Appendix I.

